  "icd10_code": "I50.22",
  "code_display": "Chronic systolic heart failure",
  "guideline_citations": [
    {
      "url": "https://www.cms.gov/files/document/fy-2027-icd-10-cm-coding-guidelines.pdf",
      "quote": "The codes in category I13, Hypertensive heart and chronic kidney disease, are combination codes that include hypertension, heart disease and chronic kidney disease. Assign codes from combination category I13, Hypertensive heart and chronic kidney disease, when there is hypertension with both heart and chronic kidney disease. If heart failure is present, assign an additional code from category I50 to identify the type of heart failure.",
      "source": "ICD-10-CM Official Guidelines for Coding and Reporting FY 2027"
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "The chart contains an explicit assessment: 'heart failure with reduced ejection fraction, currently active' and a documented ejection fraction of 30%, which confirms chronic systolic (reduced ejection fraction) heart failure. No negation, family history, screening, hypothetical, or resolved language appears in the mention windows. The guideline excerpt supports assigning an I50 code to specify the type of heart failure when present. The evidence is direct and current, warranting acceptance of the specificity upgrade to I50.22.",
